{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"sediment-filched-icefish","creation_channel":"mcp","description":"## Observation\nGitHub test.yml run 44390588952 (workflow_dispatch on main 9bef6894937), job `sweep (py3.14t)` 135106845268, step \"Run the default suite\": 1 failed, 21,237 passed.\n\n`tests/unit/test_mcp_idle_heap_release.py::test_finished_background_job_does_not_keep_its_memory - AssertionError: idle process kept 272 MiB after its last job finished (baseline 2224 MiB, before release 2499 MiB)`\n\nThe commit under test (9bef6894937, a case-only eval-spec rename plus a workflow edit) does not touch MCP memory release. The test was added by closed bug unmedical-stational-chrysalis (e152-4009).\n\n## Not established\n- Whether it fails on every py3.14t run (a platform limit: the free-threaded build's allocator may not return freed heap the way `release_freed_heap()` expects) or only intermittently. Next check: the job history of `sweep (py3.14t)` for this test.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Root cause identified with evidence (deterministic on free-threaded builds vs intermittent).\n- [ ] The test passes on the py3.14t sweep, or the release mechanism is fixed for free-threaded builds; no retry-until-green.\n","id":"27fa-79cf-59c7-4db6","parent_id":"","priority":3,"tags":["ci","flaky-or-platform"],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"test_mcp_idle_heap_release fails on the py3.14t (free-threaded) sweep: idle process keeps ~272 MiB"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1795037763359188043,"uuid":"a6c8c56a-0108-4509-9478-22fbe935f5da"}